  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, there is no evidence to exploit, so the priority is establishing a maximally informative baseline. Config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most robust configuration in the space: it uses a standard linear dimensionality reduction (PCA-2000), a single profile, and no aggregation or fusion, minimizing the number of confounded design choices. This gives a clean RNA-only performance floor that will serve as the reference point for every subsequent experiment—allowing us to isolate the marginal contribution of multiprofile aggregation, alternative RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), image modality, and multimodal fusion. Without this anchor, any multimodal or multiprofile result would be difficult to interpret because we would not know how much of the performance comes from each design axis. It is the single most informative first experiment under a limited budget."
